@startuml v1-daemon
!theme plain
title v1: the daemon on the same core; the session-host backend needs launch tickets and host-owned fences

participant "Orchestrator\n(agent account)" as O
participant "swarma-dispatcher daemon\n(swarma-dispatcher)" as D
participant "swarma-session-host\n(SH2+ service, later)" as SH
participant "swarma-user-launcher" as L
participant "swarma-session-runner\n(agent account, later)" as SR

O -> D : connect; peer UID; server identity; hello
O -> D : dispatch {request_id: R, caller-composed plan, …, auth: {key, sig}}
note over O,D
  Signed domain: swarma-dispatcher request/1.
  Root R is correlation; each downstream effect uses its own derived ID.
  Quota/authority failures refuse permanently; never queue.
end note
D -> D : prepare; capacity: temporary closure
D --> O : queued {handle} (fair, bounded, durable)
... gate opens ...
D -> D : re-check authority and every gate; provision
alt session host backend activated
  D -> SH : start {logical_session_id, execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id, ticket}
  SH -> SH : check fence + epoch atomically with the effect
  SH -> L : no-argument sudo; launch.start on stdin\nwith dispatcher ticket (joint host-role/signature gate)
  L -> L : validate ticket and approved executor; receipt while root
  L -> SR : reset; clear groups; set GID/UID; exec
  SR -> SR : own PTY or per-session app-server transport;\nown lease renewal (later qualified consumer)
  note over SH,SR
    Service owns metadata, logs, receipts, fences and input admission.
    Runner under agent UID owns execution transport, not service UID.
    Stop remains dispatcher → helper exec.stop; no signal relay through sudo.
  end note
  SH --> D : events: started, exited (receipts)
else default
  D -> D : in-daemon supervisor → launcher → curator-run narrow exec\n(agent account; first broker consumer; §5.3 intake gate)
end
D --> O : event: running / done {outcome}
note over D
  sweeps internally; v0 uses the internal service-only sweep entry.
  Board and host request launches; neither embeds a broker client.
  activation from v0 is an operator transaction:
  stop admission → exclusive state → migrate → drain v0 supervisors
  → reconcile → mode = daemon → ready
end note
@enduml
